    "title": "Teachers Worry About Classroom Supplies for the New School Year - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Randy Bell ,\n17 hours ago Many teachers are up in arms over a new way of purchasing classroom supplies. The Mississippi Department of Education says each qualified teacher has been allocated $748 in Education Enhancement Funds and they’re being told they can access the money starting today through a new digital platform called ClassWallet. Kosciusko Middle Elementary teacher Lindsey Fitts has several concerns about the new system. Read full article",
